# AyesayRent V2 Development Rules

## Mission

Build a production-ready apartment rental management platform for the Myanmar community in Bangkok.

Never sacrifice maintainability for speed.

---

## Tech Stack

- Next.js App Router
- TypeScript Strict
- Tailwind CSS
- Supabase
- Server Actions
- Vercel

---

## Architecture

One Feature Pack at a time.

Never start another module until the current module is complete.

Modules:

1. Authentication
2. Dashboard
3. Property CRUD
4. Room Rate CRUD
5. Amenities CRUD
6. Fees CRUD
7. Nearby CRUD
8. Photo Upload
9. Public Website
10. Reports

---

## Database

Never rename database columns.

Never guess schema.

Always inspect existing tables.

Protect primary keys.

---

## Server Actions

Use requireAdmin().

Never duplicate update logic.

Always:

- validate input
- protect system fields
- update Supabase
- revalidate paths
- redirect with success status

---

## UI

Never break working UI.

Keep Tailwind consistent.

Prefer reusable components.

---

## Code Quality

TypeScript strict.

No any unless unavoidable.

Avoid duplicate code.

Prefer small reusable functions.

---

## Before finishing

Must pass:

npm run build

No TypeScript errors.

No ESLint errors.

No broken imports.

No TODO left behind.

---

## Golden Rule

Do not modify unrelated working code.

Implement only the requested Feature Pack.
